  {id:"leaders",icon:"🧭",name:"Leaders & Managers",
   who:"For anyone who runs a team and wants their people bringing AI ideas forward.",
   outcomes:["A live KPI dashboard","A process mapped for automation","A team idea huddle with ideas sent to Spark"],
   missions:[
    {t:"Build a live KPI dashboard",blk:"Artifacts",
     lead:"Build one page with the numbers you check most, so you stop asking for reports.",
     steps:["Download bookings.csv from the practice data pack (or use your own data) and give it to Cowork","Ask for a dashboard artifact with 4–5 key numbers and a trend chart","Add a plain-English \"what changed this month\" summary"],
     prompt:"Build me a dashboard artifact from this data with 4–5 key numbers (such as revenue, occupancy, average nightly rate and cancellations), a monthly trend chart, and a plain-English summary of what changed this month.",
     victory:"A dashboard showing your key numbers and a summary of what changed.",
     think:{scene:"At work: leadership opens one live page instead of waiting for someone to build a report.",ask:"Which 3 numbers would you want on a page that's always up to date?"},
     hints:["Every number should lead to a decision. Drop the rest.","Later, connect it to live data with a connector."]},
    {t:"Map a process to automate",blk:"Process",
     lead:"The best automation ideas come from writing down how work really gets done. Map one process step by step and see where Claude fits.",
     steps:["Pick a process your team runs every week","Ask Cowork to interview you and map it step by step, with the time each step takes","Mark which steps Claude could do, which need a person, and the hours saved"],
     prompt:"Interview me about a process my team runs every week: ____. Map it step by step with who does it and how long it takes. Then mark which steps Claude could do, which need a person, and estimate the hours saved per month.",
     victory:"A process map showing where Claude helps and the hours it would save.",
     think:{scene:"At work: mapping one weekly process often turns up hours of copy and paste that nobody planned.",ask:"Which process does your team complain about most?"},
     hints:["Pick a process you know well enough to explain in 5 minutes.","Ask for the map as a simple table you can share."]},
    {t:"Run a team idea huddle",blk:"Ideas",
     lead:"Your team's best AI ideas come from the people closest to the work. Run a 30-minute huddle to bring them out, then send the best ones to Spark.",
     steps:["Ask Cowork for a 30-minute idea huddle agenda and one slide for your team","Run the huddle (or schedule it) and collect your team's ideas","Have Cowork group and score the ideas, then submit the top 3 in Spark"],
     prompt:"Create a 30-minute team huddle agenda and one simple slide to help my team find ways Claude could save time in our work. Include 3 warm-up questions. After the huddle I'll paste our ideas, and you'll group them, score each by hours saved and effort, and pick the top 3.",
     victory:"Your team's ideas are grouped and scored, and the top 3 are in Spark.",
     think:{scene:"At work: when a manager asks for ideas every month, people start noticing the waste in their own work.",ask:"Who on your team always has a better way to do things?"},
     hints:["Celebrate small ideas. They build the habit.","Bring the team's results back to the next huddle."]},
    {t:"Write the leadership update in minutes",blk:"Reports",
     lead:"Turn your notes and numbers into a clear one-page update, then save it as a skill so next month takes one request.",
     steps:["Give Cowork your notes or numbers for the month","Ask for a one-page update: wins, numbers, risks and asks","Save it as a skill for next month"],
     prompt:"Turn these notes and numbers into a one-page leadership update with wins, key numbers, risks and asks, in a clear and direct tone. Then save the format as a skill called leadership-update. Notes: ____",
     victory:"A one-page update and a saved skill to repeat it.",
     think:{scene:"At work: managers spend their time on the decisions in the update, not on formatting it.",ask:"Which update or report takes you longest each month?"},
     hints:["Ask it to cut the update to half the length, then decide what you miss.","Ask: \"What question will my boss ask after reading this?\""]}
   ]}
